\newlabel{fig:24-twr}{{23.1}{276}{The worked example. The fund's good year was earned on \$1,000 and its bad year on \$2,200, so the investor's money-weighted return is $-0.7\%$ a year while the fund reports $+3.9\%$}{figure.caption.77}{}}
